llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a sign-extended add is not widened in instruction selection (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for `(i64)(a + b)` with a no-wrap
32-bit add used as an address: r250560 (llvm-project bbd524496ccf,
2015-10-16, first release LLVM 3.8) made X86's DAG combine promote
sext(add nsw) to an add of extended operands so that the add folds into
the address. The base keeps the add in 32 bits and extends its result
(`inc eax; cdqe`) at 108 sites of the game region (round 214B's census:
one-sided). 0xb34440 and 0xb34470 are equal to the base in the prebuilt
3.7.1's module and first lost in 3.8.1's; their IR is the same in both. No
source form reaches a combine made at instruction selection. With the
combine taken back both compile to the base's bytes, four functions of the
module change and no matched game row changes.

diff -ru a/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLowering.cpp b/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLowering.cpp
--- a/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLowering.cpp
+++ b/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLowering.cpp
@@ -32878,6 +32878,10 @@
     return SDValue();
 
   bool Sext = Ext->getOpcode() == ISD::SIGN_EXTEND;
+  // PS4: a sign extension stays after the 'add nsw' it extends, as before r250560
+  // (bbd524496ccf, first in 3.8); its promotion is not taken.
+  if (Sext)
+    return SDValue();
   bool NSW = Add->getFlags()->hasNoSignedWrap();
   bool NUW = Add->getFlags()->hasNoUnsignedWrap();
 
